<!-- A test game that uses every feature of the format.
     Every line has a unique marker word (ALPHA, BRAVO…) so tests can look for it. -->

# Components {#components}

- 60x [[card]] — ALPHA
  - 40x [[number card]]
  - 20x [[action card]]
- 1x [[board]] — BRAVO {4+p}
- {+expo} 10x [[expo card]] — CHARLIE
  - 4x [[rocket]]
  - 6x [[comet]]

![The box](media/box.png)

# Setup {#setup}

1. Shuffle the [[cards]]. DELTA
2. Deal {2p: 9 | 3-4p: 7 | *: 5} cards to each player. ECHO
3. {+expo} Shuffle in the [[expo cards]]. FOXTROT
4. {2p} Remove the [[action cards]]. GOLF
5. Place the [[board]] in the middle. HOTEL {4+p}
6. Agree on a target score:
  | Players | short | long |
  |---------|-------|------|
  | 2-3p    | 50    | 80   |
  | 4-5p    | 40    | 60   |

  INDIA, attached to the target-score step.
7. JULIET is the last step.

| Hand size | 2p | 3p | 4-5p |
|-----------|----|----|------|
| Cards     | 9  | 7  | 5    |
| {+quick} Quick hand | 6 | 5 | 4 |

## Two-player rules {2p}

KILO only for two players.

## Expansion setup {+expo}

LIMA only with the expansion.

# Play {#play}

! MIKE is a key rule.

- {-quick} NOVEMBER without the quick variant.
- {+quick} OSCAR with the quick variant.
- PAPA has a nested note:
  > QUEBEC is the note.
- A [[comet]] shows up in ROMEO.

{3-5p} SIERRA for three to five players.

TANGO is written with \{escaped\} braces and a \[[literal]] bracket.

```
UNIFORM is code: {2p} [[not a ref]]
```

# Glossary {#glossary}

Card
: The basic piece. VICTOR

Number card
:
  - WHISKEY first point
    - XRAY nested point
  > YANKEE note inside a definition.

{+expo} Rocket
: ZULU rocket text.

Comet {+expo}
: COMET-TEXT with a [[rocket]] reference.
  ## Comet details
  AFTER-HEADING text in the definition.

Action card
: ACTION-TEXT {+quick: (quick) | *: (normal)}.
